# Baseline Widely available: the features interoperable across the core browser
# set for at least 30 months. Browserslist resolves this query itself, so the
# target is stated in the same terms the compatibility decisions are made in
# rather than as a hand-rolled version list that drifts out of step with them.
#
# This is the floor for what may be used *unguarded*, not the floor the site
# works at. Popover, @starting-style, scroll-driven masking and view transitions
# all sit behind a feature query or a runtime check, so engines below this line
# still get a usable page - they are simply not what the linter reasons about.
#
# eslint-plugin-compat reads this. With no config at all it fell back to
# `defaults`, which put Opera Mini in the target set and turned every result
# into a warning about requestAnimationFrame.
baseline widely available
